# No API key needed for maps -- the branch location picker and the
# "nearby branches" distance sort on stock transfer requests run on
# Leaflet + OpenStreetMap (see src/lib/maps.ts), which is free and works
# out of the box.

# Mobile money / card payments -- these are NEVER VITE_ vars (that would
# bundle them into the browser). They are Edge Function secrets, set with
# the Supabase CLI, not here. Which gateway is actually live is decided by
# GATEWAY_PROVIDER in src/lib/payments.ts, not by which of these are set --
# both can be configured at once (e.g. while trialling a switch).
#
# Pesapal (see supabase/functions/pesapal-payment):
#   supabase secrets set PESAPAL_ENV=sandbox
#   supabase secrets set PESAPAL_SANDBOX_CONSUMER_KEY=... PESAPAL_SANDBOX_CONSUMER_SECRET=...
#   (going live later: set PESAPAL_LIVE_CONSUMER_KEY/SECRET, then flip
#   PESAPAL_ENV=live -- the sandbox keys stay set and usable throughout)
#
# pawaPay (see supabase/functions/pawapay-payment) -- mobile money only, no
# card support:
#   supabase secrets set PAWAPAY_ENV=sandbox
#   supabase secrets set PAWAPAY_SANDBOX_API_TOKEN=...
#   (going live later: set PAWAPAY_LIVE_API_TOKEN, then flip PAWAPAY_ENV=live)
#   Also register this callback URL in the pawaPay dashboard (Developers ->
#   Callback URLs) for Checkouts/Deposits/Payouts/Refunds -- one URL for all:
#     https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/pawapay-payment?action=callback
